# Copy to .env for local use (git-ignored). Read by vite.config.ts only; never injected into the browser bundle.
#
# Backend that `npm run dev` and `npm run preview` forward /health (and any path listed in backend-proxy.ts) to.
# Must be an http(s) URL on this computer (127.0.0.1, localhost or [::1]) because the proxy can attach your token to
# its requests (see PAI_DEV_TOKEN_FILE).
# Default when unset: http://127.0.0.1:8765, the address the backend listens on when PAI_HOST and PAI_PORT are unset.
# Set this when the backend runs with a different PAI_PORT.
# PAI_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
#
# Development only. Absolute path of a file holding a backend bearer token, normally the file you gave the backend as
# PAI_TOKEN_FILE. The dev and preview proxy reads it for every request and sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>` to the
# backend, so a plain browser tab on the dev server is signed in the way the kiosk's session cookie signs in the kiosk.
# Put the path here, never the token itself. Unset: requests go out without credentials and the page shows
# "No valid session". Never read by `npm run build`; the production bundle contains neither the path nor the header.
# PAI_DEV_TOKEN_FILE=/absolute/path/to/pai-token
